  <data name="HelpText" xml:space="preserve"><value>Classic commands: hide or restore ordinary executable commands, and add or edit your own commands. Core actions, delegated commands, and dynamic extensions remain read-only.

Compact menu: hide or restore supported app handlers for your account. Commands sharing a handler change together. Built-in Windows actions are protected. Explorer may cache changes until your next sign-in.

Scope: common file, folder, drive, and background registrations in the 64-bit registry. File-type-specific commands, Send to, and New submenus are not included.

System entries: run the executable as administrator when you want to edit supported machine-wide commands. Windows may still protect individual keys.

Undo: each change is recorded before writing. Undo works newest first and preserves unrelated or newer edits. Backups are in your LocalAppData/MenuCraft/History folder. Keep this folder to retain recovery history.

Visibility can vary by selection and application. App updates may recreate their own entries. Reopen the menu after a change; if Explorer caches it, sign out and back in when convenient.</value></data>
